    "A": "$8-\\frac{9 \\pi}{4\\left(9+\\pi^{2}\\right)}$",
    "B": "$8-\\frac{4 \\pi}{9\\left(4+\\pi^{2}\\right)}$",
    "C": "$8\\left(\\frac{1+\\pi^{2}}{9+\\pi^{2}}\\right)$",
    "D": "$8-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (A)\nAns. (Bonus)\n\nSol. $\\quad \\mathrm{f}_{\\mathrm{a}}(\\mathrm{x})=\\tan ^{-1} 2 \\mathrm{x}-3 \\mathrm{ax}+7$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\nf_{a}^{\\prime}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+4 x^{2}}-3 a \\geq 0 \\\\\na \\leq\\left(\\frac{2}{3\\left(1+4 x^{2}\\right)}\\right)_{\\min .} \\text { at } x= \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\\\\na_{\\max }=\\bar{a}=\\frac{6}{9+\\pi^{2}}\n\\end{array}$$\n$$\\mathrm{f}_{\\overline{\\mathrm{a}}}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{\\pi}{4}-3 \\frac{6}{9+\\pi^{2}} \\frac{\\pi}{8}+7=\\tan ^{-1} \\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{9 \\pi}{4\\left(\\pi^{2}+9\\right)}+7$$\n7. Let $\\beta=\\lim _{\\mathrm{x} \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\alpha \\mathrm{x}-\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{3 \\mathrm{x}}-1\\right)}{\\alpha \\mathrm{x}\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{3 \\mathrm{x}}-1\\right)}$ for some $\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}$. Then the value of $\\alpha+\\beta$ is :\n(A) $\\frac{14}{5}$\n(B) $\\frac{3}{2}$\n(C) $\\frac{5}{2}$\n(D) $\\frac{7}{2}$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (C)\nAns. (C)\nSol. $\\beta=\\lim _{\\mathrm{x} \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\alpha \\mathrm{x}-\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{3 \\mathrm{x}}-1\\right)}{\\alpha \\mathrm{x}\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{3 \\mathrm{x}}-1\\right)}$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\beta=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1+\\alpha x-\\left[1+3 x+\\frac{9 x^{2}}{2!}+\\ldots . .\\right]}{(\\alpha x) \\frac{\\left(e^{3 x}-1\\right)}{3 x} 3 x} \\\\\n\\beta=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{(\\alpha x-3 x)-\\frac{9 x^{2}}{2!}-\\ldots \\ldots .}{3 \\alpha x^{2}}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nFor existence of limit $\\alpha-3=0$\n$\\alpha=3$\nLimit $\\beta=\\frac{-3}{2 \\alpha}$\n$\\beta=-\\frac{1}{2}$\nNow,\n$\\alpha+\\beta=\\frac{5}{2}$\n8. The value of $\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2 \\frac{\\mathrm{~d}}{\\mathrm{dx}}\\left(\\log _{\\cos \\mathrm{x}} \\operatorname{cosec} \\mathrm{x}\\right)$ at $\\mathrm{x}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ is\n(A) $-2 \\sqrt{2}$\n(B) $2 \\sqrt{2}$\n(C) -4\n(D) 4\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (D)\nAns. (D)\n\nJEE Exam Solution\nwww.esaral.com\